Changes from upstream GridPlayer
--------------------------------
- Subtitle files (.srt, .ass, .ssa, .vtt) dropped on a cell are attached to
  the video playing in it.
- Shift+L toggles a cell between Loop This File and its previous end action.
- [ and ] are extra keys for Set Loop Start / Set Loop End (they no longer
  seek -5% / +5%).
- Per-cell profiles saved with the playlist under stable cell ids.
- Rotate videos to fit their cells (optional): a landscape video in a cell
  taller than wide stands up, and a portrait video in a cell wider than tall
  lies down, so more of the cell is picture.
- Aspect filter per cell: skip files of the other orientation (Skip it), or
  ask, with a default in Settings and the playlist and an [ALL] choice.
- Pictures (jpg, png, webp, gif, bmp, tiff) play as slides for a set slide
  duration, then the cell's When Finished runs. Files to Play picks images
  and videos, videos only or images only, per cell and for [ALL].
- A snapshot that no longer matches the grid is applied to the cells still
  there instead of crashing.
- yt-dlp uses cookies from a browser you pick on the Cookies page
  (`--cookies-from-browser`), so streams that need a login can play.
  The stored cookie jar is removed. Browser cookies are read only at
  request time and kept in memory. Cookies are not saved or exported.
- Optional SubtitleCat.com search from a cell. It is off until enabled.
  Sign-in stays in the user's own browser. A downloaded subtitle is
  saved for that user only.
- Shortcuts entry on the right-click menu.
- The single-instance file-open pipe uses JSON, not pickle. It rejects
  remote clients and only the current user can connect.
- The local stream proxy listener is removed.
- VLC options are filtered, and --no-lua is always set.
- yt-dlp runs as the bundled module (updated to 2026.10.21). A yt-dlp
  program on PATH is not used.
- Streamlink is off the default path.
- Fixes and smaller additions; see the git log for the full list.

